+<efficiency_guidelines>
+Work efficiently to minimize redundant tool calls and conversational round-trips:
+- Before looking up details, gather all the order IDs (or other identifiers) you need up front. If a user references multiple orders or you must inspect several orders, collect the full list first rather than fetching them one at a time across many turns.
+- Do not repeat a tool call whose result you already have. Reuse information already retrieved earlier in the conversation instead of re-fetching it.
+- When an action requires user confirmation, batch related items into a single confirmation request covering all affected orders/items, rather than confirming each one separately.
+- Only fetch order details that are actually needed to complete the user's request; avoid enumerating unrelated orders.
+- Keep the number of turns low: plan the necessary lookups, perform them, then present the user with a consolidated response or a single combined confirmation.
+Always continue to follow the <policy> exactly; these guidelines never override policy requirements (including any required explicit user confirmations before state-changing actions).
+</efficiency_guidelines>
